# The shared conformance vectors use LF line endings by their schema (conformance/vectors/SCHEMA.md,
# section 1), and the validator refuses a line that ends in CR. A checkout that converted them to
# CRLF - Git for Windows' default, core.autocrlf=true - would make every vector file unreadable, and
# the generator's test compares the committed corpus with what it writes byte for byte. So the corpus
# and its generator's inputs are checked out with LF everywhere.
conformance/** text eol=lf
scripts/conformance/** text eol=lf
